# Golden endpoint policy (gated)

Golden LLM cycles are a **sparse label-discovery** tool. Continuous corpus learning is Loop A + nightly Maude (see `rl-calibration.mdc`).

## Do

- One endpoint at a time after `node2a.clinical_observational.inhaled` stays ≥90% on trustworthy confirmed labels.
- Prefer next node2a row: `node2a.clinical_observational.oral` (then other observational routes / case_study).
- Always: `SKIP_PDF_FETCH=1`, `GOLDEN_FULL_SUBNODE_REINGEST=0`, `GOLDEN_HANDOFF_CLAUDE=0`, endpoint-scoped guard (`--endpoint-id`).
- On Fly: `--sqlite-path /data/cannabis_papers.db` (or pull first). Populated SQLite only.
- On guard fail: **stop** — audit labels (study_type / population_sex) before another Maude pass; do not blind-patch to match noisy LLM labels.
- On guard ≥90% with audited labels: limited reingest + push only.

## Do not

- `AUTO_ADVANCE=1` across golden rows unattended
- Default full-subnode reingest (`GOLDEN_FULL_SUBNODE_REINGEST=1`)
- Parallel multi-endpoint golden runs
- Promote RCT/prospective LLM labels onto observational endpoints without audit

